      "extract": "A major goal of nuclear physics is to understand the stability, structure, and reactions of nuclei as a consequence of the interactions between individual nucleons. This is an extremely challenging many-body problem, exacerbated by the fact that we do not know in detail what the interactions are. Quantum chromodynamics, the fundamental theory for strong interactions, is so difficult to solve in the nonperturbative",
