      "extract": "The GFMC method [@C87; @C88] projects out the exact lowest-energy state, $\\Psi_{0}$, for a given set of quantum numbers, using $\\Psi_0 = \\lim_{\\tau \\rightarrow \\infty} \\exp [ - ( H - E_0) \\tau ] \\Psi_T$, where $\\Psi_{T}$ is an initial trial function. If the maximum $\\tau$ actually used is large enough, the eigenvalue $E_{0}$ is calculated exactly while other expectation values are generally calculated neglecting",
