      "extract": "Most of the key nuclear reactions in primordial nucleosynthesis [@NB00] and solar neutrino production [@A+98] involve only the $A \\leq 8$ nuclei. Many of these are electroweak capture reactions that are difficult or impossible to measure in the laboratory. With the high-precision few-body methods, such as PHH and Faddeev, or new effective field theory treatments, the reactions to s-shell final states have been",
